      "text": "Journey to the West, Chapter 47, Two Tang Monks."
    },
    {
      "i": 2,
      "start": 11.0,
      "end": 14.0,
      "text": "The Taoist had vanished."
    },
    {
      "i": 3,
      "start": 14.0,
      "end": 18.0,
      "text": "Wukong ran outside and shocked into the air."
    },
    {
      "i": 4,
      "start": 20.0,
      "end": 23.0,
      "text": "He looked in every direction."
    },
    {
      "i": 5,
      "start": 23.0,
      "end": 25.0,
      "text": "Where did the Taoist go?"
    },
    {
      "i": 6,
      "start": 25.0,
      "end": 26.0,
      "text": "Ask the monkey."
    },
    {
      "i": 7,
      "start": 27.0,
      "end": 30.0,
      "text": "Then he heard a shout from inside the palace."
    },
    {
      "i": 8,
      "start": 30.0,
      "end": 32.0,
      "text": "There are two Tang monks."
    },
    {
      "i": 9,
      "start": 32.0,
      "end": 33.0,
      "text": "cried Bajai."
    },
    {
      "i": 10,
      "start": 37.0,
      "end": 39.0,
      "text": "Wukong flew back inside."
    },
    {
      "i": 11,
      "start": 42.0,
      "end": 46.0,
      "text": "Two Tang monks stood side by side."
    },
    {
      "i": 12,
      "start": 46.0,
      "end": 48.0,
      "text": "We can't tell them apart."
    },
    {
      "i": 13,
      "start": 48.0,
      "end": 49.0,
      "text": "Said Wu Jing."
    },
    {
      "i": 14,
      "start": 49.0,
      "end": 51.0,
      "text": "They look exactly alike."
    },
    {
      "i": 15,
      "start": 52.0,
      "end": 54.0,
      "text": "Which one of you is the real Tang monk?"
    },
    {
      "i": 16,
      "start": 54.0,
      "end": 55.0,
      "text": "Asked Wu Kong."
    },
    {
      "i": 17,
      "start": 56.0,
      "end": 57.0,
      "text": "I am."
    },
    {
      "i": 18,
      "start": 57.0,
      "end": 58.0,
      "text": "Said one."
    },
    {
      "i": 19,
      "start": 58.0,
      "end": 60.0,
      "text": "The other monk glared at the first one."
    },
    {
      "i": 20,
      "start": 60.0,
      "end": 61.0,
      "text": "No, I am."
    },
    {
      "i": 21,
      "start": 62.0,
      "end": 64.0,
      "text": "The first monk looked at Wu Kong."
    },
    {
      "i": 22,
      "start": 65.0,
      "end": 66.0,
      "text": "Don't believe him Wu Kong."
    },
    {
      "i": 23,
      "start": 66.0,
      "end": 68.0,
      "text": "I am the real Tang monk."
    },
    {
      "i": 24,
      "start": 69.0,
      "end": 70.0,
      "text": "Don't believe him."
    },
    {
      "i": 25,
      "start": 70.0,
      "end": 71.0,
      "text": "Said the other monk."
    },
    {
      "i": 26,
      "start": 72.0,
      "end": 73.0,
      "text": "I am the real Tang monk."
    },
    {
      "i": 27,
      "start": 75.0,
      "end": 78.0,
      "text": "Angry Wu Kong pulled out his iron bar."
    },
    {
      "i": 28,
      "start": 80.0,
      "end": 82.0,
      "text": "Which one of you is the real Tang monk?"
    },
    {
      "i": 29,
      "start": 82.0,
      "end": 83.0,
      "text": "Tang monk."
    },
    {
      "i": 30,
      "start": 83.0,
      "end": 87.0,
      "text": "Both Tang monks fell to their knees shaking with fear."
    },
    {
      "i": 31,
      "start": 87.0,
      "end": 89.0,
      "text": "Don't hit me."
    },
    {
      "i": 32,
      "start": 89.0,
      "end": 90.0,
      "text": "They both cried."
    },
    {
      "i": 33,
      "start": 91.0,
      "end": 93.0,
      "text": "The monkey sighed."
    },
    {
      "i": 34,
      "start": 93.0,
      "end": 95.0,
      "text": "He turned to Bajai and Wu Jing."
    },
    {
      "i": 35,
      "start": 95.0,
      "end": 97.0,
      "text": "What can we do?"
    },
    {
      "i": 36,
      "start": 99.0,
      "end": 101.0,
      "text": "I have an idea."
    },
    {
      "i": 37,
      "start": 101.0,
      "end": 103.0,
      "text": "Said Bajai smiling."
    },
    {
      "i": 38,
      "start": 103.0,
      "end": 105.0,
      "text": "But you won't like it."
    },
    {
      "i": 39,
      "start": 105.0,
      "end": 106.0,
      "text": "What is it?"
    },
    {
      "i": 40,
      "start": 106.0,
      "end": 107.0,
      "text": "Asked Wu Kong."
    },
    {
      "i": 41,
      "start": 108.0,
      "end": 112.0,
      "text": "The two Tang monks should recite the tight headband spell."
    },
    {
      "i": 42,
      "start": 112.0,
      "end": 114.0,
      "text": "Said the pig."
    },
    {
      "i": 43,
      "start": 114.0,
      "end": 119.0,
      "text": "Only the Tang monk, Guan Yin, and Buddha know the spell."
    },
    {
      "i": 44,
      "start": 119.0,
      "end": 123.0,
      "text": "Well, no right away which Tang monk is fake."
    },
    {
      "i": 45,
      "start": 123.0,
      "end": 126.0,
      "text": "You just want to see me in pain."
    },
    {
      "i": 46,
      "start": 126.0,
      "end": 128.0,
      "text": "Said Wu Kong."
    },
    {
      "i": 47,
      "start": 128.0,
      "end": 130.0,
      "text": "Then he sighed."
    },
    {
      "i": 48,
      "start": 130.0,
      "end": 132.0,
      "text": "But it is a good idea."
    },
    {
      "i": 49,
      "start": 133.0,
      "end": 136.0,
      "text": "Bajai and Wu Jing stood near the monks."
    },
    {
      "i": 50,
      "start": 137.0,
      "end": 141.0,
      "text": "Master, recite the tight headband spell."
    },
    {
      "i": 51,
      "start": 141.0,
